[]	1. What use are statues/boulders?

statues may contain spellbooks (but this is too rare and not worth
    bothering about).

statues may come to life.

the presence of statues may denote an interesting level/environment.

statues may polymorph into boulders.

boulders are a pain (but not insurmountable) ...

[]	2. What is Explore Mode?

a special mode that allows you to play and die at your discretion.
when you start in this mode you also get a wand of wishing.  you can
enter that mode during play (once entered you cannot get out) by using
the "X" command, i think (check the on-line help).

[]	3. What is Wizard Mode?

a special mode that allows you to play-test the game for debugging
purposes.  it is very powerful (i.e. has additional commands to allow
for forcing things to happen or come into existence, etc.) and will
ruin the real enjoyment of the game for non-developers.  don't do
this at home ...

[]	4. On NetHackPlus version 3.0 patchlevel 9 for the Macintosh.  How
[]	does one engage Explore mode and How does one engage Wizard Mode?

i'm not familiar with NetHackPlus 3.0 pl9 ...

there is a mac NetHack 3.0j pl10 which has a supplemental plus
version for (lack of) memory management reasons.  engaging wizard or
explore modes is documented in the accompanying manual.  for more
details on (mac) nethack 3.0j pl10 (and if you can)

anonymous ftp linc.cis.upenn.edu (or 130.91.6.8)
cd pub/NH3.0/mac

there are 5 files there and you'll want at least:
README.mac
nh30j.doc

